WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.295
- So I love you.

00:00:01.295 --> 00:00:03.000
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.220
While I was in quarantine with my parents,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.750
and I wasn't able to
do standup every night,

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.370
which is like, I didn't even realize

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.290
was a way I get my feelings out.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.123
- 100%, yeah.

00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:11.956
- It's like, even though

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:13.470
I'm maybe not talking about
the feeling I'm having-

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.303
- It's your outlet though

00:00:14.303 --> 00:00:17.373
- I could scream about whatever
the joke is and get it out.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.037
And then it was bubbling up,
and I just, one day was like,

00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:22.710
"I gotta get a karaoke machine."

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.840
And I just ordered one
to my parents' house

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.370
and started singing karaoke.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.780
I would get coffee, eat breakfast

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.700
and then go out and sing three songs

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.650
by myself in my parents' living room,

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.210
just to like get my feelings out

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.043
songs that would really-
- [Kelly] Oh my god!

00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:35.880
- Encapsulate how I was feeling.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.130
So I was singing "Because
of You" every day

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.430
because that song's about your dad.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.301
- In your parents house (laughs).

00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:43.134
(audience applauding)

00:00:43.134 --> 00:00:43.980
- When I found out that song was about...

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.630
'Cause I remember being
obsessed with that song

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.463
in a way that was like,

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.417
"Why does this hit me in a different?"

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:50.910
'Cause I always thought it was about a guy

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.560
like a romantic song.
- No.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.437
- And then I was like,

00:00:53.437 --> 00:00:54.810
"I gotta find out what
this song was about."

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.897
And I looked into it and I was like,

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:58.530
"That's why, it's about your dad."

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.840
- And that's why you're-
- That's it, yes.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.430
- It's your therapist (indistinct).

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.200
- I was belting that out.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.720
I did a lot of "A Moment Like This."

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.440
But I did the version of you
winning on "American Idol"

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.273
that I've always-

00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:12.630
- So you're crying through it?

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.800
- Yeah, 'cause I just needed to cry,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.943
let's be honest.
- You're so funny.

00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:16.950
Oh my God.
- I just cried the whole time-

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.870
- I'm picturing your parents
upstairs in their house

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.125
going, "Do you think
she'll leave eventually?"

00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:22.100
(audience laughing)

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.940
- It was not cute, you're so right.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.440
They were just like, "Is she okay?"

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.620
Because it was just the only way I could,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.850
I was so depressed and I just-

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.990
- Crying feels good.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.920
- Just singing and crying,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.900
I did not realize how therapeutic it was.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.420
And I think so many people are
insecure about their voices,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.620
and so they won't sing.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.471
But I gotta tell people it's so good-

00:01:41.471 --> 00:01:42.304
- It feels good.

00:01:42.304 --> 00:01:43.137
- I think it's therapy,

00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:44.550
and I think that it's an untapped thing

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.750
that people need to get into more,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.458
of just belting out songs.

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:49.983
- Yes exactly, I made a living off of it.

00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:50.940
(audience laughing)
- Yeah.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.620
- No, but it started out for me.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.910
And I don't know if it
started out this way for you,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.710
but it literally started out as poetry

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.260
'cause I had a hard time communicating,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.685
still working on it.
- Yes.

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.230
(audience laughing)

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.640
- But anyway, so I started writing

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.980
and then it turned into song.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.760
- But this is the thing, Kelly.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.020
I feel the same way,

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.610
I have a hard time communicating as well,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.320
and that's why I think I went to stand up

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.240
because I could go get on
stage with the microphone

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.510
and mask the things I
wanted to say with jokes.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.343
- 100%.

00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:17.700
- And now I'm trying to do songwriting,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.120
and I'm struggling so much
'cause it's so sincere

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.560
that, you know, when I say a joke,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.060
it might be a sincere thought,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.620
and then I'm like, "But I'm joke."

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.930
But I'm not kidding, that's
not really how I feel.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.370
- You just can't do
that, you're not kidding.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.990
It's just sad, you just stay there.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.370
- Yeah, but isn't that
so vulnerable to be like,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.451
- Yes.

00:02:33.451 --> 00:02:34.890
♪ We were walking in the sand ♪

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.308
- It's just like what?

00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:37.980
(audience applauding)
- We're walking in the sand,

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.134
are you in Greece?
- I don't know, that's the-

00:02:39.134 --> 00:02:40.821
(audience applauding)

00:02:40.821 --> 00:02:41.977
- I love that (laughs)

00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:44.160
- It's just I really
struggle with songwriting,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.460
and I'm interested to hear

00:02:46.538 --> 00:02:50.220
how you get in that space where
you don't feel ridiculous.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.160
- I don't know about you, but
are you good, (indistinct),

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.670
being in a room and you
plan it on Tuesday at five,

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.503
you're gonna write a song.

00:02:57.503 --> 00:02:58.560
Like I know a lot of people in Nashville

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.670
like, a lot of my friends do that.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.950
And I'm like, "I can't
plan to be inspired."

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.080
So I don't write well
with people in the room.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.430
- No, well-
- I write on my own.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.450
If you see my name, it's usually

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.160
I did the lyrics melody on my own.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.320
- Oh right.
- Generally, yeah.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.700
- I did a tour with Young Thug,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.040
and every single day he was on the studio

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.140
and he never told anyone to be quiet.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.880
Like the mic was next to the computer,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.750
he never had a booth,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.000
and he just like let whatever
was happening happen,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.890
and he just did all his songs like that.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.350
So I guess I took a chapter out of that

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.320
and I've never put
pressure on myself anymore.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.153
I just do whatever it really is, whatever-

00:03:29.153 --> 00:03:30.730
- You really okay with the vulnerability.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.563
- 100%.

00:03:31.563 --> 00:03:32.396
- (indistinct) WhatsApp on you phone.

00:03:32.396 --> 00:03:33.240
- I feel like I get in the studio, yes.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.650
- Is that where you put all the lyric-

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.679
- Yes, notes and voice
notes, totally hack my phone.

00:03:37.679 --> 00:03:38.512
(audience laughing)

00:03:38.512 --> 00:03:40.167
But don't (laughs).

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.207
- Please don't.
- I've been hacked before.

00:03:43.207 --> 00:03:45.690
(laughs) It was like 80
something songs of mine,

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.770
I got hacked on my computer,

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:49.484
and they were all demos
and I was like, "Oh wait."

00:03:49.484 --> 00:03:51.270
(audience laughing)

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.620
It's like someone, the earth,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.240
like everyone on earth reading your diary

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.430
like that wasn't filtered, it was fun.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.830
- You would have rather than
found nudes, you're like,

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.630
- Well, I don't have those.
- "That's less vulnerable."

